    "# Assignment 0 — Setup & GitHub\n",
    "\n",
    "**Goal:** ensure your Python environment is ready and create a GitHub repo to submit future work.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Tasks (complete all of these)\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Install Python (3.10+ recommended) and a Jupyter-friendly environment (e.g., Anaconda, Miniconda, VS Code + Python extension, or JupyterLab).\n",
    "2. Create a GitHub account (https://github.com) if you do not already have one.\n",
    "3. Create a **private** repository named something like `iSci-Python-2025`.\n",
    "4. Add your instructor and TA as **collaborators** with at least read access:\n",
    "   - Instructor GitHub: stoutm1 (stoutm1@mcmaster.ca)\n",
    "   - TA GitHub: _fill in provided username_\n",
    "5. In this notebook, run the cell below after editing the variables to print a short blurb about you (name, interests, goals).\n",
    "6. Commit this notebook to your new private repository and **push** to GitHub (see the support lecture video for instructions)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Submission:** a link to your private repo, containing this completed notebook."
